{{!-- The confirmation dialog a queue entry's removal goes through. On a listing page it is filled
      in per row by the shared .list-delete-btn handler (static/js/ui.js); the detail page renders
      it for its one entry through the params. The form returns to `currentUrl`; the route sends
      a removal that came from the entry's own page to its list instead.
        {{> queue_job_actions}}
        {{> queue_job_actions removeAction="/admin/queues/submit/jobs/x/remove" removeName="Hello"}}
      Params:
        removeAction - the removal URL, when the page is about one entry (optional)
        removeName   - what to call that entry in the dialog (optional)
      Expects `crumb` and `currentUrl` in the view context. --}}
{{#> ui/confirm-modal id="removeJob" title="Remove from the queue" action=(when removeAction removeAction "/admin/queues") formId="removeJobForm" submitLabel="Remove"}}
<p class="mb-2">Remove <strong class="delete-target-name">{{removeName}}</strong> from the queue?</p>
<p class="mb-0 text-base-content/70 text-sm">It will not run and cannot be brought back. A message removed here is gone for good; a webhook delivery removed here is never sent.</p>
<input type="hidden" name="next" form="removeJobForm" value="{{currentUrl}}">
{{/ui/confirm-modal}}
